      {
        "number": 8,
        "internalPageId": 8,
        "title": "We normally use simple present tense to talk about our family and relatives. See the following chart and check out the examples.",
        "visibleTexts": [
          "We normally use simple present tense to talk about our family and relatives. See the following chart and check out the examples.",
          "Statements Questions Negative statements 1. We have a big family Do you have a big family? No, I don’t have a big family. 2. John is my brother Is John your brother? No, John is not my brother. 3. David is my uncle’s son. Is David your uncle’s son? No, he is not my uncle’s son.",
          "Even when we talk about this topic, the grammar rules must be respected. To Be – works alone. Other verbs – use auxiliaries."
        ],
        "links": [],
        "media": [
          {
            "url": "https://docs.google.com/slides-images-rt/AE1YXSaR1sTe8YS76yCqqGxAnZpCgrWSiFyFytB3ytk9smHTfmWkOG2qyUNmr7hG3Wy4u9H6zUcWbLnurS99cjJ823xYkfS6CrWwYXK5uf77g8dGZXgf7do_PuLL5FpMxm8ZmXBhUh1sTGkPU4ri1tjAGbMrcjlOsHd566R4JKwSiuj74SSIzsY1ZL-_gTD9=s2048",
